{
  "analysis": "We are at a fresh shell in /app with no prior commands run. The video exists at /app/video.mp4, but we have not yet inspected it or verified available tools. The next step is to gather metadata and tool availability before extracting frames for OCR.",
  "plan": "Run a focused inspection batch: list /app, identify the video file, check ffmpeg/tesseract/python availability and versions, and get video duration/dimensions/frame rate with ffprobe. This will determine whether we can proceed directly with frame extraction and OCR or need to install tools.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -lh /app\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "file /app/video.mp4\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which ffmpeg ffprobe tesseract python3 convert magick || true\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ffprobe -v error -show_entries format=duration:stream=width,height,r_frame_rate,nb_frames -of default=noprint_wrappers=1 /app/video.mp4\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "tesseract --version 2>&1 | head -1\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "Only /app/video.mp4 and python3 are currently available. ffmpeg/ffprobe, tesseract, and ImageMagick are not installed. We need a way to decode the video and OCR the Zork text. First, check Python packages and OS/package manager availability, then decide whether to install/use Python-based decoders and OCR or install system tools.",
  "plan": "Inspect Python version and installed modules, check for pip/apt, and see if useful packages like cv2, PIL, numpy, pytesseract, or moviepy are already available. Also check apt availability in case we need to install ffmpeg/tesseract.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 --version\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which pip3 pip apt-get apt || true\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 - <<'PY'\nmods = ['cv2','PIL','numpy','pytesseract','moviepy','imageio','ffmpeg','av','skimage']\nfor m in mods:\n    try:\n        __import__(m)\n        print(m, 'OK')\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(m, 'NO', type(e).__name__, str(e)[:80])\nPY\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /etc/os-release 2>/dev/null || true\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The system is Ubuntu 24.04 with python3 and apt available, but no ffmpeg, tesseract, ImageMagick, or relevant Python imaging/OCR packages. To extract frames from the video and OCR the Zork terminal text, we need to install decoding and OCR tools. The next step is to update apt package indexes and install ffmpeg, tesseract-ocr, and imagemagick.",
  "plan": "Run apt-get update, then install ffmpeg, tesseract-ocr, and imagemagick. These provide frame extraction and OCR capabilities. After installation, verify versions and inspect video metadata with ffprobe.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get update\n",
      "duration": 20.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get install -y ffmpeg tesseract-ocr imagemagick\n",
      "duration": 60.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which ffmpeg ffprobe tesseract convert\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ffprobe -v error -show_entries format=duration:stream=width,height,r_frame_rate,nb_frames -of default=noprint_wrappers=1 /app/video.mp4\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

